th, but the growth is more stable.\r\n\r\nFor example, I tested by increasing the iteration count to 5000 (larger than the cache limit) and ran it with a fixed array size and got:\r\n```\r\n0.4.24 0.4.24\r\ni=0: 127.640625\r\ni=500: 138.46875\r\ni=1000: 140.53125\r\ni=1500: 140.59375\r\ni=2000: 145.265625\r\ni=2500: 145.28125\r\ni=3000: 147.28125\r\ni=3500: 147.953125\r\ni=4000: 147.953125\r\ni=4500: 147.96875\r\ni=5000: 148.0\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is sort of the behavior you would expect from an LRU cache, so I would only be concerned if the memory growth is unbounded.\r\n\r\nYou mentioned in the other ticket:\r\n\r\n> my model has varying input sizes and needs to reestimate all parameters regularly\r\n\r\nThis would mean you are likely to have a lot of cache misses and would end up fully utilizing the cache space without benefiting much from the cached values.","created_at":"2024-02-16T03:32:56Z","event":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/19429#issuecomment-1947704010","id":1947704010,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/19429","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc50F5rK","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1947704010/reactions"},"updated_at":"2024-02-17T00:40:11Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1947704010","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7884451?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jacoblubecki/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jacoblubecki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jacoblubecki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jacoblubecki/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jacoblubecki","id":7884451,"login":"jacoblubecki","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODQ0NTE=","organi